# SWE-Review-Bench (MVP)

Evaluate whether LLM reviewers can locate buggy code in real SWE-bench Lite
instances without access to any oracle information (issue text, fix patch,
failing tests, or ground-truth line numbers).

## Scope (Round 1, MVP only)

- 20 instances sampled from `princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Lite` (seed=42)
- 2 LLM reviewers: Claude Sonnet (`claude-sonnet-4-5`) and `gpt-4o-mini`
- 1 static baseline: union of filtered Ruff and Pylint warnings
- Outputs: `results.csv`, `summary.csv`, one bar chart

Hybrid reviewers, self-critique, calibration, Pareto curves, and the Verified
split are explicitly out of scope.

## Setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env  # fill in API keys before Milestone B
pip install -e .[dev]
```

Windows users: GNU `make` is not installed by default. Use the underlying
commands directly (see `Makefile` for the canonical command list).

## Smoke test (Milestone A)

```bash
python -m swe_review_bench.run --smoke-test
```

Loads one instance, clones its repo, checks out the base commit, parses the
fix patch into oracle sites, reads the touched files, and asserts that no
oracle information leaks into the reviewer-facing payload. No LLM calls and
no CSV writes happen at this stage.

## Full run

Available after Milestone D lands:

```bash
python -m swe_review_bench.run --n 20 --tolerance 3
```

## Layout

```
swe_review_bench/
  run.py            CLI entry point (typer)
  config.py         env loading + Config dataclass
  data/             dataset loading, repo retrieval, oracle extraction
  reviewers/        Reviewer ABC, LLM client, static baseline, cache
  scoring/          line-range matching, hit-rate / FP / precision@k
  reporting/        CSV export, bar chart
  utils/            paths, hashing, JSON I/O
tests/              unit tests
outputs/            generated CSVs, chart, failures log
.cache/             cloned repos and LLM response cache
```

## Hard rules

- The reviewer prompt never contains the issue, fix patch, failing tests, or
  oracle line numbers.
- API keys are loaded only from `.env` and never logged.
- `git clone` is the only network call to GitHub. No API, no crawling.
- Instances that fail clone or checkout are logged to `outputs/failures.jsonl`
  and skipped; the run continues.
